  "term": "callosal",
  "definition": "Callosal refers to the fibres that pass through the callosum to connect matching areas of the two cerebral hemispheres. In the historical source, these fibres are described as undergoing secondary degeneration after cortical injury, extending toward the corresponding region on the opposite side.",
